{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789405806,"nonce":"BFKvGCyX8pYj0VCfePQspdc97aQ=","title":"Python: str.split copied the rest of the string once per piece","message":"`zb_str_split` cut each piece with `substring` and then replaced the\nhaystack with a `substring` of everything after the separator, so a\nsplit of a 460 KB text into 60,000 tokens copied 14 GB and took 29 s.\n`string_index_of` also decoded the whole haystack on every call.\n\nFix: the split keeps a byte position and finds the next separator from\nit with a new primitive, `$String$index_of_from` (`zb_str_index_of_from`),\nwhich searches the bytes from the position without decoding; pieces\nare cut with `zb_str_bytes`. The same split takes 40 ms.","files":null}]}